20.text:
On the arbitrarily chosen $+$ strand put $A=0^{5}$ and $B=1^{5}$ and write a
fixed orientation meiosis as

\begin{equation*}
r_{k}(a,b)={\rm pref}_{k}(a){\rm suff}_{>k}(b),\qquad 0\le k\le 5,
\end{equation*}
left block from the first homologue, right block from the second.
On the $+$ strand

\begin{equation*}
{\cal H}_{1}=\{r_{k}(A,B):0\le k\le5\}
          =\{0^{k}1^{5-k}:0\le k\le5\},
\end{equation*}
the $n+1=6$ monotone $0\to1$ thresholds
$00000,00001,00011,00111,01111,11111$.  Every $F_{2}$ chromosome is a
member of ${\cal H}_{1}$ and can be written $a=0^{i_{a}}1^{5-i_{a}}$,
$b=0^{i_{b}}1^{5-i_{b}}$.

For an $F_{2}\to F_{3}$ meiosis

\begin{equation*}
z_{k}(a,b)={\rm pref}_{k}(a){\rm suff}_{>k}(b)
\end{equation*}
is again monotone if $i_{a}\ge k$ or $i_{b}\le k$ and otherwise

\begin{equation*}
z_{k}(a,b)=0^{i_{a}}1^{\,k-i_{a}}0^{\,i_{b}-k}1^{5-i_{b}},\qquad 
i_{a}<k<i_{b},
\end{equation*}
i.e. a $0^{*}1^{*}0^{*}1^{*}$ word.  Hence a $+$ strand $F_{3}$ gamete
has at most one $1\to0$ descent.  Up to the trivial monotone cases a
non monotone $F_{3}$ gamete is uniquely coded by a strictly increasing
triple

\begin{equation*}
0\le i_{a}<k<i_{b}\le5,
\end{equation*}
and

\begin{equation*}
N_{nm}= \#\{i_{a}<k<i_{b}\}=\binom{6}{3}=20
\end{equation*}
four run mosaics

\begin{equation*}
0^{i_{a}}1^{k-i_{a}}0^{i_{b}-k}1^{5-i_{b}}
\end{equation*}
are obtained.  With the six monotone thresholds which persist from
$F_{1}$

\begin{equation*}
|{\cal H}_{F_{3}}^{+}|=n+1+\binom{n+1}{3}=6+20=26
\end{equation*}
different $+$ strand haplotypes can be carried by an $F_{3}$ chromosome,
the six $0^{i}1^{5-i}$ $F_{1}\to F_{2}$ words and the $20$
$0^{i}1^{k-i}0^{j-k}1^{5-j}$ $0\!-\!1\!-\!0\!-\!1$ two generation
recombinants.  In diploid terms this is

\begin{equation*}
N_{\rm ord}=26^{2}=676,\qquad
N_{\rm unord}=\frac{26\cdot27}{2}=351
\end{equation*}
ordered and unordered $F_{3}$ autosomal genotypes on the chosen strand.
The $20$ words are the genuinely new $F_{3}$ haplotypes; the six
monotone words are the $F_{2}$ gamete pool.

Remark.  With the strict interior obligate break $1\le k\le4$ the two
telomeric regenerations $k=0,5$ are lost.  Then
${\cal H}_{1,int}=\{0^{i}1^{5-i}:1\le i\le4\}$ and

\begin{equation*}
{\cal H}_{3,int}^{+}=\{0x_{2}x_{3}x_{4}1:x_{i}\in\{0,1\}\},
\qquad |{\cal H}_{3,int}^{+}|=2^{\,n-2}=2^{3}=8,
\end{equation*}
viz. $00001,00011,00101,00111,01001,01011,01101,01111$, four $F_{1}$
monotones and four genuine $F_{2}\to F_{3}$ recombinants.  This is the
usual $2^{\,n-2}$ interior–cut form, $8^{2}=64$ ordered and
$8\cdot9/2=36$ unordered diploid $+$ strand genotypes, the $26$–haplotype
end–inclusive count stripped of the $k=0,5$ telomeric cuts. ∎

